Rāma hears din and sends Jāmbavān to aid Hanumān --- Jāmbavān marches to west gate with bear army --- Returning Hanumān meets Jāmbavān and turns toward Rāma --- Hanumān reports Indrajit killed weeping Sītā before their eyes --- Rāma swoons falls like severed tree as monkeys sprinkle water --- Lakṣmaṇa embraces Rāma and calls dharma useless unseen --- Lakṣmaṇa praises wealth as root of friends rites and virtues --- Lakṣmaṇa bids Rāma rise and vows to fell Laṅkā with arrows